              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#indexed_monoidal_category Indexed monoidal category
          %p
            An
            %strong indexed monoidal category
            is a kind of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi MonCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{op} \to MonCat
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functors"} strong monoidal functors
            between them. We write this as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\mapsto (C^A, \otimes_A, I_A)
          %p
            By the usual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_A
            can also be “Grothendieckified” into an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"}> external tensor product
            ”
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊠
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \boxtimes\colon C^A \times C^B \to C^{A\times B}
          %p
            defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\boxtimes N = \pi_2^\ast M \otimes_{A\times B} \pi_1^\ast N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            and the fibration itself a strong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is regarded as equipped with its
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal structure
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+fibration"} monoidal fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_A
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \boxtimes
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\otimes_A N = \Delta_A^\ast (M\boxtimes N)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman08"} Shulman 08
          %h3#Closed Indexed closed monoidal category
          %p
            If all the fibers are not just monoidal but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+categories"} closed monoidal categories
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            morphisms are not just strong monoidal but also strong
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+functors"} closed monoidal functors
            %em closed monoidal category
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman08"}> Shulman 08, def. 13.1
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman12"} Shulman 12, theorem 2.14
          %p
            If in addition all fibers are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            one might also call this a system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+contexts"} Wirthmüller contexts
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"} six operations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} duals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
