          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of indexed monoidal category has been rediscovered many times by different people in different contexts. Some references include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                M. F. Gouzou and R. Grunig,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibrations relatives
            %li
              %p A. Asperti and A. Corradini. A categorical modal for logic programs: indexed monoidal categories. In:J.W. de Bakker and W.P. de Roever, Ed. REX Workshop, 110–137, Lecture Notes in ComputerScience, Vol. 666. Springer Verlag, New York-Berlin, 1993.
            %li
              %p G. Amato and J. Lipton, Indexed categories and bottom-up semantics of logic programs. Lecture Notesin Computer Science, Vol. 2250. Springer Verlag, New York-Berlin, 2001
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pieter+Hofstra"}> Pieter Hofstra
                , Federico De Marchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Descent for Monads
                %strong 16
                24 (2006) 668–699. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/16/24/16-24abs.html"}> tac:16-24
                )
            %li#Shulman08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Framed bicategories and monoidal fibrations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/20/18/20-18abs.html"} TAC
            %li#Shulman12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Enriched indexed categories
                %strong 28
                (2013) 616-695 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.3914"}> arXiv:1212.3914
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/21/28-21abs.html"} tac:28-21
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/traces"} traces
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
            in indexed monoidal categories is in
          %ul
            %li#PontoShulman12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality and traces in indexed monoidal categories
              %strong 26
              23 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.1555"}> arXiv:1211.1555
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/23/26-23abs.html"} tac:26-23
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2011/11/traces_in_indexed_monoidal_cat.html"} blog
          %p
            This also presents a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            calculus for indexed monoidal categories, extending that for monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrines"} hyperdoctrines
            in
          %ul
            %li#BradyTrimble98
              Geraldine Brady,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+string+diagram+calculus+for+predicate+logic"} A string diagram calculus for predicate logic
              (1998)
          %p which is made rigorous in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"} Kate Ponto
